 \"type\": \"data-context\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"You don't understand. I'm not a spanish citizen, I'm a foreigner resident, whose resident permit is attached to the job contract. I cannot just found a company and leave my job as soon as I find some sponsorship here, my residence will void the very same moment. And my contract prohibits me from doing two jobs at the same time, which being founder is. I am just a half-human here, if not less (I'll have to pitch it in a language I barely speak, etc.)\",\n        \"type\": \"text\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\nthe exact `type` and format is an item for discussion, we can even leave both `text` + `data` if needed for some reason, but I believe we may cut them, I do not see clear reason to preserve it, so run $openspec-explore for this whole idea. Also, I believe we should not retroactively change existing parts in the database and add text value, chats will lose this data this time, it is acceptable.",
