          "type": "user",
          "text": "so, I've taken a look into the database and `messages.parts` shape and what's stored, and I do not like how our system-reminders are stored there. Right now they are stored like this:\n\n```json\n[\n    {\n        \"data\": {\n            \"v\": 1,\n            \"form\": \"snapshot\",\n            \"runId\": \"c2ab9cd9-0dab-416c-abec-9ce52f711d92\",\n            \"payload\": {\n                \"instant\": \"2026-08-25T04:13:39.795Z\",\n                \"timeZone\": \"Europe/Madrid\"\n            },\n            \"producer\": \"temporal\"\n        },\n        \"type\": \"data-context\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"You don't understand. I'm not a spanish citizen, I'm a foreigner resident, whose resident permit is attached to the job contract. I cannot just found a company and leave my job as soon as I find some sponsorship here, my residence will void the very same moment. And my contract prohibits me from doing two jobs at the same time, which being founder is. I am just a half-human here, if not less (I'll have to pitch it in a language I barely speak, etc.)\",\n        \"type\": \"text\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\nTo store the timestamp reminder, the same applies to other reminders as well. I do not like that we store a shape from which we re-build all previous reminders, because such behavior does not preserve exact message content in next turns strictly speaking:\n\nif we change the shape / format - reminder message get's modified. this leads to few cases: 1) if KV cache at provider is still warm - we invalidate it; 2) if user asks assistant to cite reminder -> it cites -> we retroactively change reminder the citation is incorrect, which rises surprisal factor and also leads to potential hallucinations in future generations\n\nI propose changing it to store the reminder text wholesale, e.g., like this:\n\n```json\n\n[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"<system-reminder>Current time is 2026-08-25T04:13+02:00 (Europe/Madrid)</system-reminder>\",\n        \"type\": \"data-context\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"You don't understand. I'm not a spanish citizen, I'm a foreigner resident, whose resident permit is attached to the job contract. I cannot just found a company and leave my job as soon as I find some sponsorship here, my residence will void the very same moment. And my contract prohibits me from doing two jobs at the same time, which being founder is. I am just a half-human here, if not less (I'll have to pitch it in a language I barely speak, etc.)\",\n        \"type\": \"text\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\nthe exact `type` and format is an item for discussion, we can even leave both `text` + `data` if needed for some reason, but I believe we may cut them, I do not see clear reason to preserve it, so run $openspec-explore for this whole idea. Also, I believe we should not retroactively change existing parts in the database and add text value, chats will lose this data this time, it is acceptable.",
